  "text": "Malik looked up. The girl beside the chair across from him wore copper-colored headphones around her neck and carried a notebook thick with tabs. Her smile was curious, not cruel. It made an accusation, Malik said. Serious one? Misplaced expense. She pressed a hand to her chest. In broad daylight? He almost smiled. Almost. She pointed at the chair. Can I sit here, or is it reserved for the audit committee? Go ahead. She slid into the seat. Nia Reynolds. Mathematical sciences. Huntsville. I like graphs when they tell the truth and people when they try to. Malik Baptiste. Actuarial science. Gulfport. I like complete introductions. That was complete. You know my major, my hometown, and my entire moral philosophy. This time, he did smile.",
